#!/bin/bash
# chronos-post-commit — DEPRECATED / no-op.
#
# Originally this squashed accumulated [CHRONOS] ticks into the real commit and
# auto-pushed, driven from the post-commit hook. That behaviour was removed:
# auto-squash/auto-push on every commit was too eager (it shipped code before the
# red-team audit, and tied the squash to `git commit`). The squash + push is now
# an explicit, user-run step:  chronos-push  (reset-soft -> summary commit -> push).
#
# This stub stays so existing post-commit shims that still invoke it keep working
# (they now do nothing here and fall through to any chained hook, e.g. red-team).
exit 0
